<title>CHINA: COSCO Pac mulls buying port terminals.</title>
<headline>COSCO Pac mulls buying port terminals.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>COSCO Pacific Ltd said on Wednesday it was considering buying port terminals from parent COSCO (Hong Kong) Group Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;It will include six port terminals in China, such as in Qingdao, Shekou, Ningbo and Yingkou in Liaoning, and another three in Asia,&quot; said Zhang Dachun, vice chairman of COSCO Pacific, in a press briefing.</p>
<p>Zhang declined to comment on the size of investment involved but said &quot;we have sufficient funds to invest in any projects if the opportunity arises.&quot;</p>
<p>Kelvin Wong, a director of COSCO Pacific said the company would expand its fleet and port terminals operation on expectation of a pick up in the shipping industry.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
